Third-party code, and it matters:

Everything this license covers is this project's own code. The libraries
vendored in vendor/ are not ours to relicense, and they stay under the terms
they were published under:

  vendor/blindpro-window-gui   GPLv3 (blindpro)
  vendor/NVGT-Helpers          GPLv3 (blindpro)
  vendor/nv-test               GPLv3 (samtupy)

They are compiled into the Windows build, so distributing windows/chess.exe
means distributing GPL-covered code: anyone you give the binary to is entitled
to its source under the same terms, and you may not put a proprietary licence
on that combination. The sound effects in windows/sounds/ui/ and the code in
this repository outside vendor/ are ours and are covered by the do-whatever
you want licence above.

NVGT, the compiler and runtime the Windows version is built with, is separate
software with its own licence, as are its plugins such as voice_command.dll.
Check their terms before shipping anything.
